:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/691"} "Palau Blaugrana, Barcelona"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/17060"} "42 from 42 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Two single-elimination pools, with winner of each pool advanced to the final. All judoka losing to the finalists in each pool advanced to repêchage pools, with the winners of the repêchage pools earning bronze medals."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The last several international championships had been spread among several " [:em {} "judoka"] ", leaving this class very open. The last two World Champions had been " [:a {:href "/athletes/33979"} "Daniel Lascau"] " (GER) in 1991 and Korea’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/33913"} "Kim Byeong-Ju"] " in 1989. But in a failure of seeding, they met in the first round, with Kim winning. Kim lost in the pool semis to Sweden’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/33380"} "Lars Adolfsson"] ", which knocked Lascau out of the medals. Adolfsson lost the pool final to America’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/34096"} "Jason Morris"] ", who faced Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/34558"} "Hidehiko Yoshida"] " in the final. Yoshida’s best international finish to date had been third at the 1991 World Championships, but he was dominant in Barcelona, winning all his preliminary matches by " [:em {} "ippon"] ". The final was no different, with Yoshida using " [:em {} "uchi-mata"] " for " [:em {} "ippon"] " over Morris at 3:35 to win the gold medal. Morris had been gold medalist at the 1987 and 1991 Pan-American Games. " [:a {:href "/athletes/33913"} "Kim Byeong-Ju"] " won one bronze medal, while the other went to France’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/33631"} "Bertrand Damaisin"] ", who defeated Adolfsson in their bronze medal match."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {}